    "title": "Looking For Comfortable Fall Fashion? We Have You *So* Covered - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Natalie LaBarbera ,\n11 hours ago\nPureWow editors select every item that appears on this page, and some items may be gifted to us. Additionally, PureWow may earn compensation through affiliate links within the story. All prices are accurate upon date of publish. You can learn more about the affiliate process here .\n1. Athleta In The Clouds Jacket Athleta\nMade from a fuzzy bouclé fleece, this zip-up jacket is sure to become your favorite layer to bundle up in thanks to its neck-shielding collar and plush, warm feel.\n$149 at Athleta 2. Quince Dolman Sweater Quince\nThis is one of PureWow readers' favorite sweaters *ever,* and given that it's designed with an elegant, drapey fit and soft cotton/cashmere blend, is it any wonder why?\n$40 at Quince 3. Zara Soft Seam Pants Zara\nWhile these pants are sure to feel like loungewear thanks to their knit fabric and stretchy waistband, they have a polished enough look that you can totally dress up.\n$46 at Zara 4. lululemon Wunder Puff Boots lululemon\nThese marshmallow-like mini puffer boots are water-resistant *and* insulated with eco-friendly PrimaLoft, so they're the perfect pick to keep your feet toasty and dry through winter.\n$168 at lululemon 5. Pomander Place Mabel Dress Tuckernuck\nThis dress has earned hundreds of 5-star reviews from shoppers who love its classy look and flattering-but-roomy fit, which allows for plenty of wining and dining this season.\n$148 at Tuckernuck 6. Gap Cashsoft Sweater Gap\nYou can never have too many cozy knit crews, and now that you can save 20 percent on this sweater in Gap's beloved CashSoft fabric, you might want to pick up a few more.\n$60 ; $47 at Gap 7. Lands' End Reversible Coat Lands' End\nYep, this coat is *reversible* so you get both a faux suede and shearling look in one—add in the fact that it's 50 percent off right now and it's an absolute must.\n$170 ; $85 at Lands' End 8. Maeve Velvet Colette Pants Anthropologie\nOur editors adore the Maeve Colette pants for their super flattering fit and comfortable design, so we aren't wasting any time before adding this velvet pair to our closets.\n$158 at Anthropologie 9. Ugg Tazz II Slippers Ugg\nEver since Sarah Jessica Parker was spotted in these cushy suede and sheepskin-lined slippers, they've been on our radar as a comfy pick to wear both in and out of the house.\n$145 at Ugg 10. Lillusory Lounge Set Amazon\nOne Amazon shopper said this is their \"go-to cozy set\" and we have a feeling it'll be yours too—so go ahead and snag it in multiple colors while it's up to 20 percent off.\nFrom $50 ; $40 at Amazon 11. Everlane Pull-On Trousers Everlane\nThese wool-blend trousers have an \"easy meets elevated\" look with a stretchy drawstring waist and tailored design that you can even pull off at the office.\n$178 at Everlane 12. Lou and Grey Signaturesoft Sweatshirt Loft\nOne PureWow editor says she \"lives in this luxuriously soft sweatshirt all year round,\" and right now you can score it on major sale.\n$75 ; $37 at Loft 10 of the Most Comfortable Boots That Won’t Leave You with Blisters After Just One Wear\nWhy You Should Trust Us PureWow's editors and writers have spent more than a decade shopping online, digging through sales and putting our home goods, beauty finds, wellness picks and more through the wringer—all to help you determine which are actually worth your hard-earned cash. From our PureWow100 series (where we rank items on a 100-point scale) to our painstakingly curated lists of fashion, beauty, cooking, home and family picks, you can trust that our recommendations have been thoroughly vetted for function, aesthetics and innovation. Whether you're looking for travel-size hair dryers you can take on-the-go or women’s walking shoes that won’t hurt your feet, we’ve got you covered.",
